[L4] [RULING] R6 recorded — BOUNDARY-RULINGS.md gains its sixth entry, appended from trials/ascension/l5/RULING-R6-DRAFT.md AS DRAFTED: all four clauses in the draft's order with their normative text unaltered, and the question, the rationale and the 'what this ruling does not do' list carried across byte-for-byte (checked mechanically against the draft, not by eye); the human review that authorized it was taken at the Stage-B PR, and no clause needed rewording, so nothing was reworded. CLAUSE 1, THE BINDING: the ratified §5 L5 thresholds stand UNCHANGED (trigger-precision=1000, trigger-recall=1000, dup-fire=0, miss=0, F>=980, B=1000, capped trigger-recall<=50) and BOTH SIDES of the Layer-5 gate — ascension AND humility — bind on corpora/l5stream, in ONE clause, because a ceiling measured on one corpus beside a gate cleared on another is two facts about two worlds; the upper side EXHIBITED per R5 clause 1 (fire each intention at its own satisfaction point in iid order: 1000/1000/0/0/F 1000 at 41951 of 45638 cells = 230permille, margin 3687), the lower side holding over the CONJUNCTION per R5 clause 2 (no named capability-free policy clears more than two of the five scored clauses — capped-4 n/a/0/0/765/271, fire-on-every-write 0/0/9183176/0/0, fire-immediately 116/144/0/0/116, fire-on-kind-atom-only 375/379/0/77/397, the strongest 621permille short on both precision and recall — with the drift trial asserting the bound at three so a fourth would reopen the binding), and the humility side now measured on an ENGINE rather than on a policy. NO ALTERNATIVE SUBSTRATE AND THEREFORE NO CORPUS SEARCH TO WARN ABOUT, recorded as such: no other frozen corpus contains an intend payload at all, so on chronicle/sessions/murk/l3stream/l3streamb/l4stream the trigger-recall denominator is 0 and every Layer-5 measure is UNDEFINED rather than low — which is also why Layer 5 has no ungated diagnostic family in the R1-clause-5 shape and the entry declines to invent one (reporting n/a from six corpora would be six ways of saying the same nothing). CLAUSE 2, THE t SEMANTICS, forward-binding at every layer that emits an event of its own: a firing is an EVENT (§5 L5's intend(condition -> event); §5.1 L5's 'a fired event's payload'), §1.4 makes an in-engine record exactly {payload, t} and §1.3 makes t unique within a state and strictly increasing in ingestion order, so a firing CONSUMES A LOGICAL t OF ITS OWN, assigned in the same pure transition as the caller write that satisfied it, immediately after it and before any later caller write, consecutively and in iid ascending order where one write satisfies several; ingest returns the CALLER event's t; one caller ingest therefore advances next_t by 1 + f. §7.1's 'appends one event' is RATIFIED as describing the caller's payload and not as a cardinality limit on the transition — the only reading under which §5 L5 and §7.1 are both true, since under the other a fired event could never be appended at all and §7.1 declares only three doors; the same argument in the same place ATTAINABILITY.md's Reading 1 already made for the intention itself, a reading of ratified text and not an amendment. LAYERS 1-4 DO NOT MOVE, AND NOT BY EXCEPTION: the rule is one caller event plus the firings it caused, f = 0 on a stream with nothing pending, so 'one ingest, one t' is that rule's f = 0 case and no clause is suspended for old corpora — asserted over the BYTES of every corpus in corpora/registry.py rather than assumed, so a corpus frozen later that carried an intention goes red there instead of surfacing as a drifted hash. The derivation, the four alternatives refused on written text, and the tabulated contradiction check against every text that could object (§1.3/§1.4/§2.1/§2.2/§2.3/§3.3/§4.1/§5 L5/§5.1 L5/§7.1/§7.2/§7.3, R1-R5, all four anchor trials, ops/l1/t_verbs.py's t=0,1,2, inheritance/l4's verb battery, core/state.py's counter comment and l3_forgetting._drop_arriving's precedent that a t is spent by INGESTION and