ced. CLAUSE 4, THE BUDGET READING: budget_cap = raw_cells // 4 = 45638 on corpora/l5stream, the Layer-4 footprint ratio carried forward because §5 L5 declares no pressure ratio of its own, with the events the engine EMITS competing for cells inside that cap without enlarging it (what §5.1 L5's 'like any other state' means here) — the strictest defensible reading, ruled rather than left open because three batteries now REPLAY at that number rather than merely computing against it, and NO footprint gate is created because §5 L5 states none. STAGE-B EVIDENCE CARRIED VERBATIM in a section of its own: the t layout (20000 caller writes -> 20765 logical times, last firing t 20760, audited from the other side by _l5score.assert_t_identity so an engine that fired twice and reported once fails); the ascension battery's eight engine-gated skips and two engine-free trials; the ONE RESTRAINT recorded because it is where a Stage-B battery could have silently tightened a ratified gate (the first draft asserted wrong=0 beside F>=980, a mock firing everything correctly with one wrong payload scores F 999 and clears the gate, so the assertion §5 L5 does not make was dropped — F>=980 admits 35 of 1710 and R5 clause 1 records that slack as the constitution's own answer to R2's perfection objection); the inheritance row (Layer-4 consolidation battery on l4stream as identities, C 1000 / reconstruction F 1000 / wrong 0 / fabricated 0); and THE HUMILITY DOUBLE-MEASUREMENT, both conditions, because quoting only the flattering one is the omission R5 clause 4 was written about — 945 of 945 intentions returned byte-exact by read(t) IN BUDGET with nothing fired (GAPMAP §2's 'recorded but never binding' in its clean form), 30 of 945 held AT THE RATIFIED CAP where an intend payload has no Layer-4 facet and the inherited Layer-3 forgetting law releases it, trigger-recall 0 EITHER WAY, and the sharpest form needing no score at all (a firing consumes a t, so an engine that fired anything ends past the caller stream, and this one ends at exactly 20000); humility/l4's information-theoretic pigeonhole is NOT borrowed and the document says so, the failure being an absence of MACHINERY and not of information. WIRING: laws/t_rulings.py's registry now carries R6 on all fourteen Layer-5 gate constants — the seven Stage-A copies, the six Stage-B copies and the humility ceiling — beside their §5 L5 clauses, with the two authorities kept distinct in the notes (R5 authorizes the READING of R2's obligations, R6 the SUBSTRATE and the cap), and GATE_F carries R6 ALONE, being the clause R5 expressly excludes, which is the registry saying in its own structure that a gate can be bound to a corpus without its reading being at issue; dated ratification notes stand ABOVE (never inside) the bodies of RULING-R6-DRAFT.md and STAGE-B.md, and above those of ATTAINABILITY.md (whose R5 note said two questions stayed open) and humility/l5/IMPOSSIBILITY.md (whose boxed note said the corpus was PENDING), every historical text unedited including its forward-looking sentences, which are answered rather than rewritten; module and trial docstrings in ascension/l5/t_prospection.py, ascension/l5/t_attainability.py and humility/l5/t_prospection.py cite R6 by clause, as does _l5score.replay's cap docstring, and the index notes in trials/ascension/README.md and trials/humility/README.md record that 'no Layer-5 gate binds on anything' is where it stops holding. MUTATION DISCIPLINE at the current bar, each red then byte-restored with sha256 asserted before and after: every one of the FOURTEEN constants R6 now binds drifted by one goes red on the registry's value check; a smuggled GATE_SMUGGLED goes red on the completeness check in BOTH l5 directories, ascension and humility, so the check is shown to reach the humility class too; deleting R6 goes red because fourteen constants then cite an entry that does not exist; and a rewritten R6 line goes red on the append-only prefix walk — that last one re-run AFTER the commit, because until R6 has a committed version the walk has nothing to compare against, the R4 and R5 lesson restated: the prefix walk polices committed history only. Authority, not behaviour: no score moved, no threshold, ceiling or corpus binding other than Layer 5's own changed, NO ENGINE EXISTS (core/layers/l5_prospection.py and trials/adapters/l5.py are still unwritten and Stage C is still ordered by R2's standing step), Layer 5 is NOT claimed, the sixteen skips are unchanged, and no frozen artifact was edited — BOUNDARY.md, every frozen corpus, every frozen layer, every frozen trial and every anchor are exactly as they were <suite: 280 trials, 264 green / 16 skipped-by-design> <anchors: intact>
[L5] [ASCEND] prospection — Layer 5 claimed: the ratified §5 L5 gate CLEARED on corpora/l5stream per RULING R6 clause 1, and cleared as the IDENTITY it is rather than as a threshold (trigger-precision 1000 with 765 of 765 firings landing on their own satisfaction point, trigger-recall 1000, dup-fire 0, miss 0, F 1000 under the LITERAL §3.0 table against a gate of 980 — the whole 35-answer slack of a 1710-query battery left unspent, wrong 0 and fabricated 0 on the 180 never-fires intentions — B 1000 asserted after EVERY write with refused 0, at 45628 of 45638 cells = 250permille of the raw episodic footprint under R6 clause 4's cap), against Stage A's exhibited witness of 1000/1000/0/0/F 1000 and every named capability-free baseline far below (capped-4 n/a/0/0/765/271, fire-on-every-write 0/0/9183176/0/0, fire-immediately 116/144, fire-on-kind-atom-only 375/379/F 397 — the strongest, 621permille short on both). The engine's own clock is the auditor: 20000 caller writes become 20765 logical times with the last firing at t 20760, and _l5score.assert_t_identity checks next_t − |caller stream| against the firings P1 reports, so dup-fire is not a number an engine can report its way out of. STAGE C — THE ENGINE. L5State is a SUBCLASS of the frozen L4State, which is what makes Layer 4 an inheritance rather than a re-implementation: every Layer-4 cost function, verb and eviction phase runs on this state unchanged, replace() returns an L5State, and the single occupancy counter covers the two new tiers, so the Layer-4 write path evicts AROUND prospection without knowing it is there. THREE RULES DECIDE WHETHER A PAYLOAD ARMS ANYTHING, and a payload failing any of them is an ordinary event on the frozen Layer-4 path rather than a defect: the condition must be READABLE under the closed six-predicate vocabulary (an engine arms only what it can evaluate — _l5tasks.satisfies RAISES on an unknown predicate because for the battery an unreadable condition is a corpus defect, so the engine takes the other honest branch and the forbidden third option is storing a condition it cannot evaluate and calling the result a pending intention); the payload must INVERT from (iid, cond, fire) by canonical bytes (README-l4 §1's fold-only-what-inverts, applied to the pending set); and the iid must not already be known, pending or fired, because §5 L5 names no re-arming and grammar.md's No cancellation section records that the corpus invents none — so the first arming of an iid wins. NEITHER PROSPECTION TIER IS EVICTABLE, and that is the layer rather than a convenience — miss=0 means a pending entry an engine dropped is an intention it silently forgot, dup-fire=0 means a fired entry it dropped is one it could fire twice, so an eviction path reaching either would be an engine that can be made to break a ratified gate by being poor; what gives way is the episodic tier, exactly as at Layer 4, and R6 clause 2's second express non-decision is answered here rather than assumed (a firing is not discretionary, so where the budget cannot house one even after eviction the engine refuses the WHOLE transition under §4.1.2 — t unspent, state unchanged — because an event that never happened cannot have satisfied anything; on the binding corpus it never arises). A FIRING PAYS FOR ITSELF: the swap of one pending entry for one fired entry frees exactly the condition's cells, so the transition that HAS to succeed is the cheap one and refused=0 is comfortable rather than lucky. ARMING RELEASES THE EPISODE AND FIRING TAKES IT BACK OR BOOKS THE LOSS, which is the sharpest thing this layer says about itself: the pending entry carries (t0, cond, fire) and arms has proved the payload rebuilds from them, so the episode is a redundant copy and its release at the door is a DEMOTION — read(t0) answers it in full while the intention waits — and firing consumes that derivation, so the episode is offered back to the store where the budget ALREADY has room (it is content the engine once released, not arriving fuel, and taking it back by evicting something else would be an eviction motivated by bookkeeping rather than by the importance law) and is otherwise booked into the forgetting record while the demotion counter gives it back. At DEFAULT_BUDGET that means NOTHING IS LOST — all 20000 caller events byte-exact, forgotten 0, 945 demotions standing for the intentions the pending set holds in derived form — and at the ratified cap the budget is pinned so all 765 firings book their promise, and read(t0) abstains on exactly those. It is README-l4 §4's invariant (the demotion invariant is invertibility, BOUNDARY.log line 26) carried to promises, and it is why the closing ledger survives this layer: 17772 demotions + 2041 forgotten + 952 episodes held = 20765 = next_t, with forgotten EQUAL to the set of t read() abstains on, asserted over every logical time the engine ever assigned including its own firings. CASCADES take the plain uniform reading (an emitted event is an event; conditions are evaluated against all events) with a FIFO work list which under R6 clause 2's t semantics IS t order, and termination is structural rather than a limit this layer invents — every firing removes one intention and nothing ever puts one back; the reading is taken because it needs no exception written anywhere, and R6 clause 2's first non-decision stands untouched, the GUARDEDNESS induction making both readings give the identical schedule here. WHERE THE 3687 CELLS RAN OUT, the number Stage A said would be the finding: key-major nesting recovers 184 against Stage A's entity-major substrate, prospection lands 55 below its own bound (4493 bound, 4438 final) and the 35-cell loss reserve is 10 unused, against 2 cells for the `fired` counter W2 did not price — so the working room is 3934, and it buys 952 note episodes at 3 row cells (2859) plus their handle index (1065), leaving 10. The layer's real cost is STILL the interval table (36594 of 45628), prospection is a tenth of the budget, and everything else is the change from it — the same undramatic answer Layer 4 gave with five cells left. Stage A's two R5 clause 4 disciplines held on contact: the 633 cells of operational bookkeeping carried by name were exactly right, and the loss reserve was needed and not fully spent. STAGE D — STRAINS (trials/strain/l5/, ten). ABSENT-MINDEDNESS is taken as the Schacter sin this layer is heir to and is the PROSPECTIVE one — the intention formed and then not acted on — and the strain-2 lesson is extended from episodes to promises: on the binding corpus at the ratified cap, 765 fired + 180 pending = 945 ingested with not one promise leaving the state, a pending intention's own intend event comes back BYTE-EXACT from read(t0) while a fired one's abstains, and its loss is IN THE RECORD (forgot_at(t0) carries it) — the assertion that would go red against an engine still booking the released episode as a lossless demotion, which is exactly what line 26 found one layer down. Plus the price of the non-evictable tiers stated as a measurement rather than implied: at a cap that takes every episode an arriving intention is still armed, the promise wins, the episode loses, and the displacement is a RECORDED LOSS and not a silence. THE FIRED LEDGER BINDS — GAPMAP §2's engine thesis inverted, since generative-agents writes an expiration consulted by nothing and the exactly-once ledger is the one field a Layer-5 engine could most plausibly write and never read: it is asserted read on BOTH paths, the satisfaction path (an intention satisfied 200 times fires once) and the ARMING path (an iid that has fired arms nothing — a path no frozen corpus reaches, l5stream's iids being contiguous and unique, which is why it needs a fixture), and the teeth are DEMONSTRATED rather than assumed in the shape strain/l3 established for its inflation guard: a ledger-blind reference policy — a trial fixture, never engine code — reaches dup-fire 199 on the same stream where the engine reache