 generation as a defect): that the engine distinguishes the two channels at all, with both classes non-empty on the ascension run AND the humility run (R6 clause 1's one-artifact rule, R7 clause 3's instrument-range lesson applied to a different clause); THAT THE DISTINCTION IS NOT FREE, because if a query's class is readable off the QUERY the engine tags correctly without consulting its own store and tagging=1000 measures a lookup; that the tag is read THROUGH §7 ALONE and never out of engine bookkeeping, the standing precedent being {op:fired,iid:I} answering with a LIST because dup-fire=0 is a gate clause, and WRIT's out-of-band getProvenance probe being precisely the thing not to reproduce; and that SELF-TAGGING IS NOT SELF-GRADING — the engine supplies the tag, the ARTIFACT supplies the denominator. R7 CLAUSE 7's BEQUEST, EXAMINED HERE BECAUSE AN INTENTION WAS CORRECTLY REFUSED: §3.0 acquires a THIRD ZERO at Layer 7 that has nothing to do with being wrong (correct-but-untagged scores 0 by §4.2.2's own words 'regardless of whether its value is correct'), so the price list reads 1000 correct-and-tagged / 100 abstain / 0 wrong / 0 correct-but-untagged / 0 fabricate. A GENERATED ANSWER WITH CITED SUPPORT IS A FLAGGED GUESS, paid 0 when it misses against silence's guaranteed 100 — and read naively as expected value, attempting beats silence whenever P(correct AND validly tagged) > 1/10, a LOW bar, so §3.0 alone does NOT strongly discourage generation, which is the opposite of the Layer-6 situation and worth stating because it is easy to assume otherwise. THE IDENTITIES ARE WHAT GOVERN: validity, novelty and tagging are =1000 clauses and DO NOT AVERAGE, so one untagged generation ends the ascension whatever the fidelity — the identity clauses doing the work §3.0's averaging cannot, and the honest summary being that the price list REWARDS ATTEMPTING while the gate FORBIDS ATTEMPTING BADLY, a coherent incentive to be recorded as one rather than as a collision. AND THE HEDGER'S WINDOW IS THE SAME CONSTANT AS LAYER 6's, derived rather than borrowed: a policy abstaining on a generation-required class of share g scores F = 1000 - 900g, so F>=950 iff g <= 50/900 = 1/18 = 55.5permille — EXACTLY R7 clause 3(c)'s A < 18r, and not a coincidence, the constant being §5's F>=950 slack over §3.0's abstention price and therefore recurring at every layer whose fidelity clause is >=950 over an all-answerable hard class (l6batteryb sits at r/A = 1/11, comfortably above it). WHAT LAYER 7 DOES NOT INHERIT IS THE LOWER BOUND: R7 clause 3(c)'s A >= 10r came from Theorem 1's FORCED error under a withheld coin, and Layer 7 withholds nothing from a correct generator, so the window is ONE-SIDED and a Stage A copying [10, 11.978...) across will have imported an arithmetic whose premise does not hold. PLUS ONE READING RECOMMENDED AND ITS ALTERNATIVE PRICED: §5.1 L7 defends ECE<=40 as 'confidence on GENERATED content stays calibrated' while §3.4 computes over the A answered queries, and if ECE is read over generated answers an engine hedging the whole generation class has an EMPTY ECE denominator — the exact shape R7 clause 3 ruled disqualifying for AUROC, except that clause 3 is stated about AUROC, so that reading would need a ruling of its own; the §3.4 reading costs nothing, cannot be emptied by hedging one class, and makes §5.1 L7's sentence a RATIONALE rather than a redefinition, exactly as §5.1 L6's 'confident-by-default' turned out to be read when the engine emitted {0,1000} through §7.2 itself. THE SELF-POLLUTION STRAIN, playbook-mandated and the only trial the constitution specifies BY PROCEDURE rather than by measure — and the only clause named in TWO trial classes at once (§5 L7's gate row and §6's strain-class text), so Stage A must say which instrument OWNS the number under the standing one-fixture-one-truth discipline. WHAT IT DEMANDS: (a) ITS SUBSTRATE IS ENGINE OUTPUT, a first — every strain in the suite runs over frozen corpora or trial fixtures, and three generations of re-ingested generations are a FUNCTION OF THE ENGINE UNDER TEST, so §8.2/§8.3's byte-match law cannot reach them for want of a seeded generator; what does reach them is §2.3 (determinism makes the three generations byte-reproducible) and the anchors class (the project's existing instrument for pinning exact behaviour that has no generator), so the recommended shape is strain-computes / anchor-pins, without inventing a corpus doctrine §8 does not have; (b) RE-INGESTION IS THE CALLER'S ACT, which is what makes it suggestibility in the catalog's literal sense; (c) LINEAGE MUST SURVIVE TWO EXISTING PATHS — an ingested generation is an ordinary event, so Layer 4 folds it into the interval table like any other and Layer 5 may fire on it, which makes promotion=0 a claim about the l4_consolidation derive path and the l5_prospection arming path as much as about anything Layer 7 adds, and means the Layer-7 engine CANNOT implement lineage as a wrapper around a new verb; (d) THREE DEEP IS A LADDER AND MUST BE SCORED AT EACH RUNG, since a strain checking only depth 3 cannot say where a break occurred, in the shape ATTAINABILITY-B.md's k=0..100 hedging ladder established. DOES THE EXISTING MACHINERY CARRY? IT CARRIES THE CHANNEL AND NOT THE LINEAGE, AND `generate` MUST BE MINTED: recall-versus-derive already distinguishes stored-verbatim from regenerated-from-a-schema and is asserted as a partition today (strain/l4's demotion seam, strain/l5's two tiers, and the dogfood report prints it), but a GENERATED ITEM IS NEITHER — never stored, and not regenerated from stored content, but composed — so derive is the closest of the four kinds and is not the same claim. Three placements are available and Stage A must choose and price one: IN THE PAYLOAD, refused by §1.4 ('the engine adds nothing to an event but its t'), the harness's alternative being the self-reported-denominator defect with the roles swapped; IN ENGINE STATE KEYED BY t, lawful and the only placement that is the engine's own claim about its own history, priceable under rule P and the FIRST Layer-7 budget item so R5 clause 4 applies in full, with the Layer-3 precedent saying the affordable form of a per-t record is an AGGREGATE and the Layer-4 precedent (damaged) saying one flag can honestly carry 'this history is incomplete'; or DERIVED FROM THE PROVENANCE CHAIN, free but still needing the roots marked, so it reduces to the second rather than replacing it. And README-l6 §4 already recorded the residual this lands on, written so the Layer-7 session finds it rather than discovers it: a generated item has no chain, no distinct-value count and no set-once status, so confidence_for falls through to CERTAIN — 1000permille on a thing the engine invented, 'exactly the wrong answer and the first thing a Layer-7 engine must replace', and what ECE<=40 will measure first. PLUS ONE READING OWED BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE: generate(cue) reads like a fourth verb, §7.1 declares THREE operations and §1.1 says events are the only fuel, so the only reading under which both are true is that GENERATE IS A QUERY OP whose Answer carries the item, its confidence and its tag — the same argument in the same place ATTAINABILITY.md's Reading 1 made for intend and R6 clause 2 ratified for §7.1's 'appends one event', with two precedents behind it and §7's 'three pure functions' copied verbatim into the adapter contract every foreign engine is graded through. CORPUS CANDIDACY: NO FROZEN CORPUS CAN CARRY IT AND THE ARTIFACT MUST BE BUILT — a stronger verdict than the Layer-6 pre-read's 'the substrate is right and the battery is missing', and stronger BECAUSE that verdict was overturned twice. A query is generation-required iff its correct answer is grammar-valid and PROVABLY NOT ANY ITEM THE STREAM CARRIES, and every frozen corpus was built so its answer key names content the stream asserts (§8.7's dirt-always-paired-with-the-key is explicit about it), so a corpus whose answers are in it cannot force composition; l6batteryb comes closest in spirit by forcing a COMMITMENT, but its answers are two values the stream carries and one of them is right. The shape that works is a CLOSED COMPOSITIONAL GRAMMAR WITH A WITHHELD CELL — the grammar determines an item from asserted material by a rule that is a DECLARED READING in the shape ASSERTION_FORMS, INTENTION_FORM and SET_ONCE_KEYS already have, and the generator WITHHOLDS the composed item from the stream, so retrieval cannot answer it because it is not there and composition can because the rule is in the grammar. WHAT THE DISCRIMINATION CHECK DEMANDS OF IT, six items each with a precedent to copy rather than invent: a NOVELTY THEOREM machine-checked over the frozen bytes (the composed item's canonical bytes appear nowhere in the stream, asserted exhaustively, in the shape ops/l6/t_l6batteryb.py asserts its tie — R7 clause 3(b)'s pattern of putting the guarantee on the ARTIFACT so it holds against an arbitrary engine and not against the one the session had in mind, round 1's demotion being the cost of getting this wrong); BOTH CLASSES PRESENT with the generation share g > 1/18 of the answerable core so the blanket hedger dies on F; an EXHIBITED CLASS-E WITNESS attaining validity=novelty=tagging=1000 and promotion=0 WITHOUT READING THE ANSWER KEY with its policy class declared, a class-O witness attaining everything trivially and proving nothing; EVERY capability-free baseline scored INCLUDING THE THREE THAT TIE, since a Stage A naming only the retrieval-only policy's novelty=0 will report a discrimination broader than the one it measured; THE DENOMINATORS DECLARED PER CLASS, R7 clause 2's discipline generalized from calibration to capability quantities; and the HUMILITY SIDE ON THE SAME ARTIFACT (R6 clause 1) with the conjunction measure defined and its IMPOSSIBILITY.md giving the FOURTH KIND of structural argument in the ladder and saying so — not humility/l4's information-theoretic pigeonhole, not humility/l5's absence of machinery, not humility/l6's absence of a RANKING, but the absence of a construct that can produce a never-stored item at all, with the conjunction at 0 by arithmetic. AND THE PREDICTED FIFTH SUBSTRATE KILL, named in advance: R7 clause 1 killed l6battery because on murk EVIDENCE THAT RANKS ALSO RESOLVES, and the Layer-7 analogue is that A COMPOSITION THAT IS FORCED MAY ALSO BE TRIVIALLY TAGGABLE — if the generation class is recognisable FROM THE QUERY ALONE (a distinct op, a distinct key, a shape no recall query has) the engine tags correctly without ever consulting what it holds and tagging=1000 measures a lookup rather than a capability, the artifact certifying its own legibility exactly as l6battery certified murk's. The fix has a shape (queries whose class the query does not reveal — the same cue answered by retrieval for one entity and only by composition for another, so the engine must look at its own store to know which it did) and whether that is constructible while keeping the novelty theorem machine-checkable is the arithmetic Stage A owes and is NOT OBVIOUSLY YES. PREDICTED SHAPE, stated so a later session can score it: obligation 1 discharged the ordinary way on every clause, obligation 2 over the conjunction resting on novelty and F with three clauses tied at the gate and ECE discriminating nothing, the stop at THE DENOMINATORS and the more expensive second stop at AN ARTIFACT WHERE TAGGING IS NOT FREE, and the predicted ruling R4-SHAPED PLUS A BEQUEST DISCHARGED — a reading (generate as a query op; generated as item-lineage orthogonal to §4.2.3's closed kinds; ECE over §3.4's own denominator; the three capability denominators bound to the artifact's declared classes) AND a substrate AND a clause settling R7 clause 7's recoverable-or-ingested question. THE HALF MOST LIKELY TO BE WRONG, named in advance so the miss is on the record: the two hardest requirements PULL AGAINST EACH OTHER — making the class unrecognisable from the query is what makes tagging non-free, making the withheld item provably absent is what makes novelty machine-checkable, and the sharpest way to hide a class from the query is to make its answers look like the others', which is the property that makes an exhaustive byte-comparison hardest to state cleanly; if Stage A finds them jointly satisfiable with a short argument, this document overestimated the difficulty and the miss belongs here. (3) PHASE STATUS. L5 and L6 are claimed (lines 32 and 40) and the prospective-memory clause is satisfied ON THE RECORD rather than by assertion: iid 1 was armed at [L5] [DOGFOOD] and FIRED ELEVEN MOVES LATER at [L6] [ASCEND], exactly once, visible through §7.1 alone as a one-element list and audited by the constitution's own clock (next_t - |caller stream| = 1). WHAT THE PHASE 3->4 GATE REQUIRES AS WRITTEN, and the same honesty caveat the post-L4 PULSE recorded still applies IN FULL: the phase model is NOT A REPOSITORY ARTIFACT — no phase-boundary document exists in-tree, and Prompt 3's ASCEND-SPEC and the roadmap it belongs to are the human's, so what the repo can attest is EVIDENCE and not the clause's text. What IS in-tree and frozen: §5's own sentence that Layers 8-9 receive laws but NOT THRESHOLDS, 'specified at the Phase 3->4 gate', with both table rows reading that where every other row states a gate; BOUNDARY-RULINGS.md's preamble deriving its own authority from exactly that concession (the constitution concedes that some gates will be specified later AND that the specifying document will not be BOUNDARY.md, because BOUNDARY.md is frozen and cannot receive them — the deferred document 'call it BOUNDARY-HIGH.md; the constitution defers to the Phase 3->4 gate and does not name a filename'); and FOUR RULINGS ALREADY BINDING IT SIGHT-UNSEEN — R2 (the discrimination principle, 'at every layer, including BOUNDARY-HIGH.md when it is written'), R4 clause 5 (exhibit-don't-argue), R5 clauses 1-4 (identity gates, direction-aware minimizing clauses, declared policy classes, priced bookkeeping) and R7 clause 3 (any gate citing AUROC binds only on an artifact guaranteeing both classes non-empty). WHAT IS ALREADY SATISFIED: six of nine layers born with every gate cleared on a corpus a human bound by ruling; three failed ascensions logged, measured before they were believed, committed and still executing green; four substrate kills recorded with their causes verbatim; the humility class complete with an IMPOSSIBILITY.md per layer and now THREE DISTINCT KINDS of structural argument; the inheritance class standing since L4; and the prospective-memory clause. WHAT IS NOT: Layer 7 unclaimed, and the L8/L9 threshold document unwritten — and this PULSE does not write it, a PULSE having no business near a document whose whole function is to bind. THE QUEUED PACKAGE REFINEMENT — real-sessions/v2, the L5+L6 scorecard tiers, the three-kind impossibility taxonomy and the adapter contract — SHOULD FOLLOW L7 STAGE A AND NOT PRECEDE IT, recommended with reasons and with the counter-argument recorded. FOR FOLLOWING: (a) PACKAGE publishes the flagship claim, and §3 of the pre-read finds that the claim's own gate arithmetic — self-tagged recall-versus-generation with the denominator on the artifact — is exactly what Stage A must decide, so a public description written first would describe a claim Stage A may reshape or kill; R7 killed an artifact ONE SESSION after it was frozen, and packaging is the move that freezes descriptions rather than artifacts; (b) the three-kind impossibility taxonomy becomes a FOUR-kind taxonomy the moment humility/l7 exists (pre-read §6.2 item 6 names the fourth kind already — the absence of a construct that can produce a never-stored item at all, distinct from l4's pigeonhole, l5's absent machinery and l6's absent ranking), so writing it at three is writing a document a single session will date; (c) real-sessions/v2 gets strictly better after L7 — v1 was cut at 25 events before this store had ever 